1. Introductiom
- Speak about what is your protype

The prototype developed was a fully interactive digital 
website designed to provide users with clear information, 
simple navigation, and a professional user experience. The purpose of 
the prototype was to demonstrate how the final website would function while
meeting user needs effectively and efficiently. The layout of the website was 
carefully designed to ensure that users can easily move between pages and locate 
information without difficulty. A clear navigation bar, organised sections, and 
interactive buttons were included to improve accessibility and usability. 
The website uses a consistent colour scheme, readable fonts, and structured 
formatting to create a professional appearance while also ensuring that users 
remain engaged throughout their experience. The prototype includes several functional elements 
that allow it to behave like a real working website rather than just a visual design. 
One of the main interactive features is the account creation and login system. Users 
are able to create an account by entering personal details such as their email address
and password. These details are securely stored within the system database, 
allowing users to sign back into their account when returning to the website. 
This feature demonstrates how user authentication and data management would work 
in the final product while also showing the importance of security and personalised 
access for users. Passwords and emails are handled carefully within the system to ensure
account information can be saved and retrieved correctly, improving the reliability and 
functionality of the website.

Another important feature included within the prototype is the shopping basket system. 
Users are able to browse products and add selected items directly into their basket using 
interactive buttons. When items are added, the basket updates automatically and the total p
rice instantly increases based on the selected products. This automatic calculation feature 
demonstrates dynamic website functionality because the system responds immediately to user 
actions without requiring the page to refresh. Users can clearly see the number of items they 
have selected along with the updated total cost, making the website more convenient and user-friendly. 
This feature improves the overall customer experience because it allows users to track their purchases easily before completing checkout.

The prototype also includes interactive forms, clickable navigation menus, responsive buttons, 
and organised content sections that help improve engagement and usability. 
Each page was designed to function smoothly and logically so users can complete 
tasks quickly and efficiently. The homepage provides users with important information 
immediately, while additional pages allow users to explore products, manage accounts, and interact with website features. 
The prototype was tested to ensure that links, buttons, and interactive elements function correctly and provide 
accurate responses when used.

Overall, the prototype successfully demonstrates the design, structure,
and functionality of the planned website. It combines professional visual design 
with practical interactive features to create a realistic representation of the final product. 
The inclusion of secure account management, automatic basket updates, responsive navigation,
and clear information layout shows that the website was designed with both functionality and
user experience in mind. The prototype effectively meets its purpose by providing users with
an easy-to-use, interactive, and visually organised digital platform that reflects the standards
expected from a modern professional website.

